# CQ-01 · frame-camera
#
# Question: From what vantage point is each scene in the corpus shot — camera
#           angle, focal length and framing?
# Persona:  P1 — generation-pipeline engineer. The camera block is what a
#           text-to-image renderer consumes, so it is the first thing a pipeline
#           reads back out of a document its gate has just passed.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §5.3.3 (`vso:CameraView`); §5.2 (`vso:viewedBy`)
# Form:     SELECT — one row per document
# Note:     The three fields are optional (§5.3.3), so each is OPTIONAL here: a
#           CameraView that states only an angle is conformant and must still
#           appear in the answer rather than dropping out of the join.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?doc ?angle ?focalLength ?framing
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?scene a vso:Composition ; vso:viewedBy ?cam .
    ?cam   a vso:CameraView .
    OPTIONAL { ?cam vso:angle       ?angle }
    OPTIONAL { ?cam vso:focalLength ?focalLength }
    OPTIONAL { ?cam vso:framing     ?framing }
  }
}
ORDER BY ?doc
